    "title": "Another winter storm causes havoc in SoCal - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Knx News 97 1 Fm ,\n7 hours ago\nA second storm hit Southern California on Tuesday night, bringing strong winds and snow.\nIn some parts of SoCal, the winds caused several downed trees. In Arlington Heights, one tree fell on a car.\nPhoto credit KNX News 97.1 FM KNX News‚Äô Jon Baird reported that a tree also knocked down part of the soundwall by the southbound 405, prompting officials to close the lanes for hours.\n@knxnews Winds raked Southern California overnight, knocking down trees and forcing the closure of the southbound 405 near Sunset after one tree fell on the soundwall.\n‚ô¨ original sound - KNX News Photo credit KNX News 97.1 FM Over in Gorman, snow was spotted on the Grapevine. A winter storm warning is in effect til‚Äô Friday morning.\nPhoto credit KNX News 97.1 FM @knxnews Drivers heading up north could be dealing with icy conditions and a winter storm warning as more rain and snow are expected on the Grapevine.\n‚ô¨ original sound - KNX News\nFollow KNX News 97.1 FM\nTwitter | Facebook | Instagram | TikTok",
    "summary": "By Knx News 97 1 Fm , A second storm hit Southern California on Tuesday night, bringing strong winds and snow. Photo credit KNX News 97.1 FM KNX News‚Äô Jon Baird reported that a tree also knocked down part of the soundwall by the southbound 405, prompting officials to close the lanes for hours. @knxnews Winds raked Southern California overnight, knocking down trees and forcing the closure of the southbound 405 near Sunset after one tree fell on the soundwall. A winter storm warning is in effect til‚Äô Friday morning.",
